    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "act": "VERDICT",
      "lane": "BOOKEND",
      "narration_text": "What smithsonian_fetch.py gets right: strictly CC0, provenance travels with every image, index-first design means fast local search without hammering the SI API, and Topaz upscale degrades gracefully when the tool isn't there. Where it bites: the index must be pre-built — that's a separate smithsonian_index.py step. And --yes auto-accepts the top search hit — use it carefully on ambiguous queries, because the ranker gets hardware right but isn't infallible.",
